# Keeps the build context (and the risk of anything sensitive ending up baked into an
# image layer) small. Mirrors .gitignore's spirit but is its own file on purpose — what
# belongs in git and what belongs in a Docker build context aren't quite the same list
# (e.g. .git/ itself should never be sent to the Docker daemon, but obviously is in git).

.git/
.gitignore
.github/

env/
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Local dev DB/media — the container gets these via docker-compose.yml volumes/env,
# never baked into the image itself.
Portfolio/db.sqlite3
Portfolio/media/
Portfolio/productionfiles/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log

.coverage
htmlcov/

README.md
LICENSE
*.md
